  <prompt>Finish the D9 viewport clip (FR-11): the Assistant transcript clips mid-row with dead whitespace when the SpaarkeAi code page mounts in the "Open in Compose" Xrm-dialog iframe. A PARTIAL fix (`SprkChat.tsx` `messageList` `min-height:0`) is ALREADY on master — so the FIRST step is a live-DOM session (via /ui-test or DevTools on the code-page iframe) to confirm D9 still reproduces after that partial fix. If it no longer reproduces, this collapses to a verification + regression-guard task (see escalation). If it still reproduces, walk the ancestor chain per the handoff diagnosis recipe and finish the remaining suspects — the `SprkChat.tsx:1432` trailing-spacer inline `minHeight = ${container.clientHeight}px` (measured before the Xrm iframe settles → dead whitespace; highest-probability), the `inputZone` (~:208–212, applied ~:2884) missing `flexShrink:0`, the `ConversationPaneChrome.tsx:50` `sprkChatFlex` wrapper — replacing any measured/fixed height with the flex chain (`flex:1; min-height:0; overflow`), tokens-only (ADR-021), with NO fixed/measured height left in the chain (that is what makes it host-proof).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React 18 + TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 makeStyles expertise on the shared SprkChat/ConversationPane subtree; disciplined about live-DOM diagnosis before editing, host-agnostic flex chains (no per-host branching), and not regressing other SprkChat consumers.</role>
  <goal>The Assistant transcript in the "Open in Compose" Xrm-dialog iframe is bounded with internal scroll and a pinned composer — no clipped rows, no dead whitespace — host-proof (no fixed/measured heights), with the full-page + widget hosts unchanged and the dialog re-bounding correctly on resize.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Defect D9 (register P4, FR-11). CRITICAL: read `projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/notes/assistant-viewport-clipping-open-in-compose-handoff.md` in full — it carries the symptom, the verified-correct app/shell chain, the root-cause hypotheses in likelihood order, the diagnosis recipe (§4), the fix pattern (§5), and the §6 verification checklist. Entry path: `sprk_document` form → "Open in Compose" → SpaarkeAi code page opens in an Xrm dialog that hosts the page in an IFRAME, so `100vh` = the iframe's inner height (smaller + settles later than a full tab) — which is why a latent chain defect shows here and not on the full page. The app-level (`App.tsx`) + shell-level (`ThreePaneShell.tsx`) chain is verified sound; the break is below the shell in the `ConversationPane → SprkChat` subtree. A PARTIAL fix — `SprkChat.tsx` `messageList` `min-height:0` — is ALREADY on master, so D9 may already be resolved: the live-DOM session confirms BEFORE any further edit. Remaining suspects if it still reproduces: (1) `SprkChat.tsx:1432` trailing-spacer inline `minHeight = ${container.clientHeight}px` measured before the iframe settles → dead whitespace (highest-probability, hypothesis 2 in the handoff); (2) `inputZone` (~:208–212, applied ~:2884) missing `flexShrink:0`; (3) `ConversationPaneChrome.tsx:50` `sprkChatFlex` wrapper. Fix pattern: every intermediate wrapper `flex:1; min-height:0; overflow:hidden`; transcript scroller `flex:1; min-height:0; overflow-y:auto`; fixed elements (header, Model row, composer) `flex-shrink:0`; NO fixed/measured height anywhere in the chain. Client-only — ships with a `sprk_spaarkeai` rebuild + `Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1`; NO BFF involvement, no atomic-window coordination.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/notes/assistant-viewport-clipping-open-in-compose-handoff.md (READ FULLY — symptom, diagnosis recipe §4, fix pattern §5, verification checklist §6)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/SprkChat.tsx (:1432 trailing-spacer inline px height; inputZone ~:208–212 applied ~:2884; messageList min-height:0 partial fix already on master)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPaneChrome.tsx (:50 sprkChatFlex wrapper)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (pane wrappers between the pane boundary and SprkChat's transcript scroller)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/App.tsx + components/shell/ThreePaneShell.tsx (verified-correct upstream chain — context, not the bug)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021" scope="the flex-chain styles">Fluent v9 makeStyles, semantic tokens only — NO hex, NO literal '1px', NO inline color; the transcript must render correctly in light AND dark theme.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the whole flex chain">NO fixed or measured heights anywhere in the chain — replace any measured/px height with the flex chain (`flex:1; min-height:0; overflow`). This is what makes the pane host-proof (Xrm dialog, full tab, widget) with zero per-host branching. MUST NOT reintroduce a measured height.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012" scope="the shared SprkChat subtree">SprkChat is a host-agnostic shared component — the fix MUST NOT regress other SprkChat consumers or the full-page/widget hosts; no per-host branching.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="deploy">Client-only change — ships with a `sprk_spaarkeai` rebuild + `Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1`; NO BFF change.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
