      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor. Read the handoff note fully (symptom, diagnosis recipe §4, fix pattern §5, checklist §6). Note the partial fix (`messageList min-height:0`) already on master.</step>
    <step order="1">LIVE-DOM SESSION FIRST (via /ui-test or DevTools on the code-page iframe): repro "Open in Compose" from a `sprk_document` with the Assistant rendering enough content to exceed the pane; confirm whether D9 still reproduces AFTER the partial fix. If it does NOT reproduce → go to escalation (verification-only + regression guard).</step>
    <step order="2">If it reproduces: walk UP the ancestor chain from SprkChat's transcript scroller toward appRoot; the first ancestor whose rendered height EXCEEDS its parent's clientHeight is the culprit. Check for a missing `flex:1; min-height:0` or an inline px height (`SprkChat.tsx:1432` trailing spacer; `inputZone` missing `flexShrink:0`; `sprkChatFlex` wrapper).</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the fix pattern: intermediate wrappers `flex:1; min-height:0; overflow:hidden`; transcript scroller `flex:1; min-height:0; overflow-y:auto`; fixed elements `flex-shrink:0`; DELETE any measured/px height (do NOT re-measure on resize — the chain makes measurement unnecessary). Fix in SprkChat if the culprit is shared; in ConversationPane/Chrome if it is a pane wrapper. Tokens-only (ADR-021).</step>
    <step order="4">Run the ui-tests below; verify §6 checklist in light + dark; if fixed in SprkChat, spot-check one other SprkChat consumer surface.</step>
    <step order="5">npm run build SpaarkeAi (production); update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Open-in-Compose modal transcript bounded"><steps><step>Navigate to a `sprk_document` record (env placeholder: https://&lt;dev-env&gt;.crm.dynamics.com → a document with SPE pointers)</step><step>Command bar → "Open in Compose"; wait for the Assistant to render suggestions so content exceeds the pane height</step></steps><expected>The Assistant transcript is BOUNDED with internal scroll, the composer is pinned at the bottom, and there are NO clipped rows and NO dead whitespace — light AND dark theme.</expected></test>
    <test name="Full-page + widget regression"><steps><step>Open the standard full-page SpaarkeAi surface (env placeholder: https://&lt;dev-env&gt;.crm.dynamics.com → SpaarkeAi code page); then the workspace/widget presentation of the Assistant</step></steps><expected>Both hosts render UNCHANGED — bounded transcript, internal scroll, composer pinned (no regression from the D9 fix).</expected></test>
    <test name="Dialog resize re-bounds"><steps><step>In the Open-in-Compose dialog, toggle the platform Expand/full-screen control on the dialog chrome</step></steps><expected>The Assistant pane RE-BOUNDS correctly to the new dialog size — guards against a reintroduced measured height (a frozen measurement would fail this).</expected></test>
    <test name="Long + near-empty conversation"><steps><step>In the modal host, render a long conversation (content ≫ pane height); then a near-empty conversation</step></steps><expected>Both lay out correctly — long scrolls internally within the bounded transcript, near-empty does not create dead whitespace.</expected></test>
    <test name="Light + dark"><steps><step>Toggle dark mode with the modal host open</step></steps><expected>The transcript + composer use Fluent v9 semantic tokens and render correctly in both themes (ADR-021).</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the live-DOM session shows D9 does NOT reproduce (the merged partial `messageList min-height:0` fix already resolved it), STOP editing the flex chain speculatively — CONVERT this to a verification-only task: confirm §6 checklist passes as-is and add a regression guard (a ui-test / assertion that the transcript stays bounded and no measured height is reintroduced). Do not make speculative flex edits with no reproducing defect.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>The `ConversationPane → SprkChat` transcript subtree exists; the partial `messageList min-height:0` fix is already on master; the remaining suspects are named in the handoff.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — finish the existing flex chain (replace a measured/fixed height with `flex:1; min-height:0`); no new component, no new host branch.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the fix the Assistant transcript clips mid-row with dead whitespace in the Open-in-Compose iframe host (P4/D9), so the modal Assistant is visibly broken and the P4 DoD cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
