  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Handoff §6: modal "Open in Compose" transcript is bounded, scrolls internally, composer pinned, no clipped rows, no dead space — light AND dark.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full-page SpaarkeAi surface unchanged (regression check).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Workspace/widget presentation of the Assistant unchanged (regression check).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dialog resize re-bounds the pane correctly (guards a reintroduced measured height).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Long conversation (content ≫ pane height) AND near-empty conversation both lay out correctly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: NO fixed/measured height remains anywhere in the chain (host-proof, no per-host branching).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If fixed in SprkChat: one other SprkChat consumer surface spot-checked and unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If live-DOM shows D9 no longer reproduces: task converted to verification-only + a regression guard added (per escalation), not speculatively edited.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Client-only — ships with `sprk_spaarkeai` rebuild + `Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1`; no BFF. SprkChat/ConversationPane is a contended spine shared with compose-r5/r6 + assistant-r3 — run /conflict-check before the PR and coordinate merge order. The live-DOM confirm BEFORE editing is load-bearing (the partial fix may already have resolved D9).

  ── COMPLETION (2026-08-18, owner live-DOM UAT) ──
  D9 CORE RESOLVED by the merged partial fix (`messageList min-height:0`): owner confirmed the "Open in Compose" transcript is now BOUNDED (internal scroll, composer pinned, no clipped rows) — the escalation's "does NOT reproduce" path. So NO speculative flex-chain edit was made.
  Owner live-DOM UAT surfaced the REMAINING piece of the handoff's dead-whitespace hypothesis 2: the pin-to-top trailing spacer (`SprkChat.tsx:1439`, sized to `container.clientHeight` on send) NEVER shrank back, leaving a large dead region after the transcript footer that clipped the last footer row (the task-023 "Refresh suggestions" affordance) at the fold in a long conversation. FIX: in the auto-scroll effect, COLLAPSE the spacer (`minHeight:0`) once real content (scrollHeight − spacer) fills the viewport; short responses keep the spacer (pin-to-top preserved). Tokens-only, host-agnostic, no measured height added. 374/374 SprkChat shared-lib tests pass. Ships with the 080 SpaarkeAi deploy; owner verifies the Refresh-row clip is gone live post-deploy.</notes>
